<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Dostoevsky returns nine weeks after starting lamotrigine; he has taken 100 mg twice daily for three weeks. He had one generalized seizure in the third week of the titration, while on 50 mg a day, after a night without sleep to finish a manuscript; a friend who was with him timed it at about two minutes and followed the seizure action plan. He has had none since reaching 150 mg a day. He has had no rash, mouth sores, or fever, and no dizziness or double vision. The sleep-deprived EEG six weeks ago was normal. He has not gambled. He has attended every weekly therapy session and is learning to spot the thoughts that lead him to chase losses. He went to two Gamblers Anonymous meetings and saw the debt counselor, who is drawing up a repayment plan. His mood is better. He has no thoughts of suicide. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Seizures</td><td>One in week three of the titration, after sleep loss; none since</td></tr><tr><td>Lamotrigine</td><td>100 mg twice daily for three weeks; no rash or other side effects</td></tr><tr><td>Gambling</td><td>None for nine weeks; therapy weekly</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>PHQ-9 6</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

